---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SourceTier from '../components/SourceTier.astro';
import ClaimStatus from '../components/ClaimStatus.astro';
import ArchivalRef from '../components/ArchivalRef.astro';
import {
  TIER_DEFINITIONS,
  CLAIM_DEFINITIONS,
  VERIFICATION_DEFINITIONS,
  WITHHELD_DEFINITION,
  PHASES,
} from '../lib/vocab.ts';

const tiers = Object.entries(TIER_DEFINITIONS) as [keyof typeof TIER_DEFINITIONS, string][];
const claims = Object.entries(CLAIM_DEFINITIONS) as [
  keyof typeof CLAIM_DEFINITIONS,
  string,
][];
const verifications = Object.entries(VERIFICATION_DEFINITIONS);
---

<Base title="Method" description="The tier system, the claim grades, and the standing rule on archival references.">
  <div class="method prose">
    <h1>Method</h1>
    <p class="method__lede">
      This page should take under two minutes. It explains the three vocabularies the whole
      site runs on: how evidence is <strong>tiered</strong>, how claims are
      <strong>graded</strong>, and what a reference number means when you see one.
    </p>

    <h2 id="claims">Claim status — four ordinal buckets</h2>
    <p>
      Every substantive claim carries a visible status, rendered with colour
      <em>and</em> an icon <em>and</em> a text label — never colour alone. There are four
      buckets and there is no fifth, and there are deliberately no confidence percentages:
      the corpus grades in ordinal buckets on purpose, and inventing &ldquo;87%
      confident&rdquo; would be false precision.
    </p>
    <dl class="deflist">
      {
        claims.map(([status, def]) => (
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <dt>
              <ClaimStatus status={status} />
            </dt>
            <dd>{def}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <h3 id="withheld">Withheld is not a fifth bucket</h3>
    <p class="withheld-note">
      <ClaimStatus status="Unknown" withheld={true} />
    </p>
    <p>{WITHHELD_DEFINITION}</p>
    <p>
      This distinction does real work. Silvestre's manner of death at Annual is
      <strong>unknown</strong> — no one has the answer. The location of Mehdi Ben Barka's
      body is <strong>withheld</strong> — someone has it. Roughly 1,800 CIA documents on the
      Ben Barka case were acknowledged in 1976 and remain undisclosed; French files remain
      classified. Filing that under &ldquo;unknown&rdquo; would be lying by taxonomy, so the
      site renders it as a separate flag that can co-occur with any status.
    </p>

    <h2 id="tiers">Source tiers — eight ordinal levels</h2>
    <p>
      Tiers are <strong>ordinal, not categorical</strong>, so they render as steps of a
      single hue ramp rather than eight colours. Darkest is
      <code>PRIMARY_ARCHIVAL</code>; lightest is <code>UNSOURCED</code>.
    </p>
    <dl class="deflist">
      {
        tiers.map(([tier, def]) => (
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <dt>
              <SourceTier tier={tier} />
            </dt>
            <dd>{def}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <h2 id="references">The standing rule on archival references</h2>
    <p>
      A reference is written out <strong>only</strong> when it can be seen in a catalogue,
      in a digitised document, or quoted verbatim by a named scholar who consulted it.
      Otherwise the entry says so, in those words, followed by the fonds a researcher should
      request.
    </p>
    <p><strong>No reference number in this corpus has been reconstructed from memory or inferred.</strong></p>

    <p class="method__demoLabel">A verified reference looks like this:</p>
    <ArchivalRef
      reference="SHD, sous-série GR 3H, 3H 314–752 (Commandement Supérieur; 1st–4th bureaux; Fes, Meknes, Marrakech, Taza, Tadla, Oujda)"
      verification="Catalogue verified"
      scope="series"
      settles="the El Herri command chain and the 1920 Zaian submission terms"
      catalogueUrl="https://www.servicehistorique.sga.defense.gouv.fr/"
    />

    <p class="method__demoLabel">An unverified one looks like this — and is meant to:</p>
    <ArchivalRef
      reference="Khénifra Bureau des Affaires Indigènes political bulletins, March–April 1921"
      verification="NOT YET VERIFIED"
      scope="series"
      request="SHD sous-série GR 3H, Territoire du Tadla, Khénifra annexe, chronological series for 1921"
      settles="how Mouha ou Hammou Zayani actually died"
    />

    <h3>What each verification value means</h3>
    <dl class="deflist deflist--tight">
      {
        verifications.map(([v, def]) => (
          <div class="deflist__row">
            <dt>
              <span class:list={['ref-token', v === 'NOT YET VERIFIED' && 'ref-token--unverified']}>
                {v}
              </span>
            </dt>
            <dd>{def}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <h2 id="phases">The ten phases</h2>
    <p>
      Phases are a <strong>sequence</strong>, not a set of kinds. They are never given ten
      categorical colours — on the timeline they alternate between two neutral surfaces,
      because ten hues would both fail colour-separation floors and imply the phases are
      categories rather than a chronology.
    </p>
    <ol class="phases">
      {PHASES.map((p) => <li><code>{p}</code></li>)}
    </ol>

    <h2 id="rules">What this site will not do</h2>
    <ul class="nots">
      <li>
        <strong>No AI summarisation, no chat.</strong> The corpus's value is that every
        claim is traceable; a generative layer destroys that in one move.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No confidence percentages.</strong> Four ordinal buckets, on purpose.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No auto-generated &ldquo;related content.&rdquo;</strong> Relations here are
        evidenced and typed. A similarity sidebar would silently assert connections nobody
        documented.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No single figure where the corpus records a range.</strong> Contested
        quantities render as ranges with their competing attributions, and a build-time
        check fails if a bare figure sneaks in.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No smoothing of the gaps.</strong> If a dossier is thin, the site says it is
        thin.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="state">The honest statement about this corpus</h2>
    <p>
      It is a source-critical synthesis of the accessible secondary and catalogue
      literature, with a precise map of where the primary evidence sits.
      <strong>It is not yet archival research.</strong> No carton has been opened.
    </p>
    <p>
      Its largest single weakness is named on every affected dossier: the Moroccan-side
      documentary base is currently zero. Ma al-ʿAynayn was a prolific author and is
      described here through European reports about him. Correcting that is the difference
      between a history of Morocco and a history of what Europeans wrote down about Morocco.
    </p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .method__lede {
      font-size: 1.0625rem;
      color: var(--ink-secondary);
    }
    .deflist {
      margin: var(--s-4) 0 var(--s-6);
      display: grid;
      gap: 0;
      border-top: var(--rule);
    }
    .deflist__row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 15rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--s-4);
      padding: var(--s-3) 0;
      border-bottom: var(--rule);
      align-items: baseline;
    }
    .deflist dt {
      margin: 0;
    }
    .deflist dd {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      color: var(--ink-secondary);
    }
    .deflist--tight .deflist__row {
      grid-template-columns: 13rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .withheld-note {
      margin-bottom: var(--s-2);
    }
    .method__demoLabel {
      font-family: var(--font-ui);
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
      color: var(--ink-muted);
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
    .phases {
      columns: 2;
      column-gap: var(--s-6);
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
    }
    .nots li {
      margin-bottom: var(--s-3);
    }
    @media (max-width: 46rem) {
      .deflist__row,
      .deflist--tight .deflist__row {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: var(--s-2);
      }
      .phases {
        columns: 1;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
